#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:5 bbfe9543bf9b44f392047b98f26d8608
msgid "Archived: Quick Start Guide for Ready-to-Fly Vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:9 5ea26739d39a455c913b146d67758c21
msgid "**ARCHIVED ARTICLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:11 0c07273f33fd4b3dbbe8067188d5727a
msgid ""
"The article is out of date (3DR replaced APM2.x with Pixhawk and the kits"
" come with everything configured out of the box). In addition, 3DR no "
"longer supplies hardware described in this article (including Iris+, "
"Solo, X8, Aero-M)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:15 69906132635145f6a329d234425e6836
msgid ""
"This page is a quick start guide for users who have purchased a "
"*3DRobotics Ready-to-Fly (RTF) multicopter* including a Pixhawk preloaded"
" with the latest Copter firmware. All other users should skip to the "
":ref:`First Time Setup <initial-setup>` section which includes the full "
"autopilot set-up and calibration instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:21 06721e06960a4823bc065cc9260247f3
msgid "Install Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:23 1b3a90dffaad47479f724094af322b20
msgid ""
"`Download the most recent Mission Planner MSI from here "
"<https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MissionPlanner/MissionPlanner-"
"latest.msi>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:25 c1f002f6008547528c0ce946f295fd85
msgid ""
"Open the Microsoft installer file (.msi) and select **Run** to run the "
"installation utility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:31 3f4a2de926964c2fb5636b484f9c5139
msgid ""
"Follow the instructions to complete the setup process (accept the license"
" terms, choose a location for the installation etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:34 e9d2f338ad134b95a4166e18858dc95d
msgid ""
"The installation utility will automatically install any necessary "
"software drivers. If you receive a DirectX installation error, please "
"update your DirectX plug-in from the `Windows Download Center "
"<https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/windows.aspx>`__. If you "
"receive the warning pictured here, select **Install this driver software "
"anyway** to continue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:41 d68c481ee819402cbf89dce27ee6d917
msgid ""
"Once installation is complete, open Mission Planner. Mission Planner "
"automatically notifies you about available updates. Please always run the"
" most current version of Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:46 d847a178a5f74434917e7fef9e145637
msgid "Connect RC receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:48 cb706c31e72641998d66addab29eb73e
msgid ""
"Is your RC receiver already connected and configured? If not, follow "
"these instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:51 a01f7177ebc143708656705af74db2bf
msgid ""
"For RC control with \\ **PWM**, connect RC receiver to APM Input Signal "
"pins using connectors to attach channel 1 to the APM signal pin labeled "
"1, channel 2 to signal pin 2, etc. You will also need to provide power to"
" the receiver by connecting a three-wire cable between the receiver and "
"the APM for one of the channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:60 a403fd38af0a47b392175854810681ee
msgid ""
"For **PPM** (all channels over one wire), use PPM jumper connectors to "
"connect Input signal pins 2 and 3 on APM and signal pins 3 and 4 on the "
"receiver. Use a 3-wire cable to connect the signal, power, and ground "
"pins for channel 1 on the receiver to the three pins labeled 1 on APM. "
"The specific pins used for the receiver may vary by model, so consult the"
" documentation on your receiver for PPM configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:70 0a7ea84a956c4127b64aeddbadbd2f76
msgid ""
"Once you've downloaded Mission Planner onto your ground station computer,"
" connect APM to your computer using the micro USB connector and APM's "
"micro USB port. Use a direct USB port on your computer, not a USB hub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:78 cdd7796bcaaa40be880a4ad190286757
msgid ""
"Windows will automatically detect APM and install the correct driver "
"software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:81 f350d99f758f429893d9ad68f31a5cac
msgid ""
"Next we'll let Mission Planner know which port we're using to connect to "
"APM. Open Mission Planner, and use the drop-down menus in the upper-right"
" corner of the screen (near the Connect button) to connect to APM. Select"
" \\ **Arduino Mega 2560** and set the Baud rate to **115200** as shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:90 2f61c7ef71af4fce9dc77a1ab10f8f4d
msgid ""
"Select \\ **Connect** (upper-right corner of the screen) to load MavLink "
"parameters to APM. Mission Planner will display a window showing the "
"progress of the MavLink download."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:97 f6d814b44a6243bea67cb533b5ed4990
msgid ""
"When the window displays **Done** and Mission Planner shows the "
"**Disconnect** option in place of Connect, your APM firmware has been "
"downloaded successfully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:104 0239ef059e4544549d5b0013ca397345
msgid ""
"Turn on transmitter. Verify that the transmitter is in Airplane mode (APM"
" needs airplane mode regardless of the platform type being piloted) and "
"all trims are centered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:108 01523abba36249d78685b0b0387edbc2
msgid "Transmitter(Mode 2): Recommended Channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:110 40ab357f9a664977bee3b14c83e53126
msgid ""
"The left stick will control throttle and yaw; the right stick will "
"control roll and pitch. The three-position switch will control flight "
"modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:114 635e367a29534e6483041ab2d21d2e27
msgid ""
"In Mission Planner, select **Mandatory Hardware** and **Radio "
"Calibration**. Click on the green \\ **Calibrate Radio** button in the "
"lower right of the window. Mission Planner will call a dialog window to "
"ensure radio control equipment is on, battery is not connected, and "
"propellers are not attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:123 ab888321839042c58941e26653662bdc
msgid ""
"Select OK; move the control sticks and toggle switches on your "
"transmitter to their limits of travel and observe the results on the "
"radio calibration bars. Red lines will appear across the calibration bars"
" to indicate maximum and minimum values. Move the Ch 5 and 6 toggle "
"switches through their range of positions (Ch 7 and 8 are not used for "
"basic operations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:130 4aa1d04d21904d5e98a72ae50bd3ce10
msgid "Your transmitter should cause the following control changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:132 8303b142646c4b3f9d2dad0b5f1dcafd
msgid "Channel 1: low = roll left, high = roll right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:134 079cc6b1892d42c8a6ddf5d3c8c4d037
msgid "Channel 2: low = pitch forward, high=pitch back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:136 14028262f74a479d99aacefefc8c3db8
msgid "Channel 3: low = throttle down (off), high = throttle up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:138 a83890431e2a4a1cb92411edc997dc93
msgid "Channel 4: low = yaw left, high = yaw right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:143 d92b3371f55c4813af33b3527f2b0a49
msgid ""
"When the red bars for roll, pitch, throttle, yaw, and radio 5 (and "
"optionally radio 6) are set at the minimum and maximum positions, select "
"**Click when Done**. Mission Planner will show a summary of the "
"calibration data. Normal values are around 1100 for minimums and 1900 for"
" maximums."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:153 47fe04415eed43cb987df15176a96cf4
msgid "Attach propellers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:155 862468c69c244d9aac60baa49755ce32
msgid ""
"Unscrew prop nuts and add propellers to motor collets with writing on "
"props facing up in relation to the sky. If you have a co-axial motor "
"configuration, make sure that the writing on the props faces up even if "
"the motor faces down. Add metal spacers on top of prop nuts if prop hub "
"measures less than 5 mm in height. Tighten prop nuts to secure propellers"
" in place. Try inserting a 2 mm (5/64) hex wrench into the hole in the "
"side of the prop nut to get better leverage when tightening prop nuts. "
"Select propellers based on motor directions. Find your frame in the "
"images below. Use pusher propellers for motors marked clockwise and "
"normal propellers marked counterclockwise. Pusher propellers are usually "
"marked \"P\" or \"SFP\" on the propeller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:177 233ff3f01cfc4053af531884b04574bd
msgid "Pre-flight information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:179 e67cd00256a94f3ab9f17b1b89dd4620
msgid ""
"Safety is the key to successful flight. Please read the \\ :ref:`Safety "
"Information Page <safety-multicopter>` before flying. Select an "
"unpopulated area to fly your copter, away from people and developed "
"areas, and always run the :ref:`pre-flight checklist <checklist>`\\ "
"before connecting the battery. Make sure to read the :ref:`Flying "
"<flying-arducopter>` page for information about arming, disarming, and "
"controlling your copter during flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:185 e45b704e4e54473b95b06911ce38c6d0
msgid ""
"When you're ready to fly, place copter on the ground facing away from "
"you. Connect fully charged LiPo battery to the power module connector "
"when you're ready to power on your copter. Follow the safe arming and "
"disarming procedure described on the :ref:`Maiden Flight <flying-"
"arducopter>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:194 6755261d797e48acb119417ced70da86
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quick-start-guide.rst:196 4979bed991534cd3b3a32415dce15dfe
msgid ""
"Try learning about different :ref:`autonomous flight modes <flight-"
"modes>` to get the most out of your Copter, including loitering and "
"running missions."
msgstr ""

